# What the build context excludes.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SECURITY BOUNDARY OF THE BUILD. A file that is not excluded is sent to
# the daemon and can be copied into a layer, where it stays readable to anyone who can pull
# the image and is not removed by deleting the file in a later layer. So the rules below are
# about what must never enter the image, not only about build speed.

# --- Secrets, absolutely ---
#
# `.env` holds the provider API keys, the session secret and the demo token. THE APP READS
# IT AT RUNTIME, from the working directory compose mounts, so the image never needs it and
# must never contain it. Excluded here AND never copied by the Dockerfile: two independent
# reasons it cannot arrive.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Any stray key, certificate or credential file, so a new one does not have to be
# remembered here.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
credentials.json

# --- Data that must not be baked in ---
#
# THE LIVE DATABASES ARE EXCLUDED; THE SQL SCHEMAS ARE NOT, AND THE DISTINCTION MATTERS.
#
# `data/store` holds two different things: the organisation database files, which are
# somebody's real answers, and `schema.sql` / `admin-schema.sql`, which the app READS AT
# RUNTIME to create and verify tables. An earlier version of this file excluded the whole
# directory, and the container then failed on every connection with
#
#   ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '/app/data/store/schema.sql'
#
# which is what an over-broad exclusion looks like: it removed the data it meant to and the
# code it did not.
#
# So: the files, not the directory. A database is excluded wherever it sits; the schemas
# ship because the application cannot start without them.
data/store/*.db
data/store/*.db-wal
data/store/*.db-shm

# `data/demo` IS DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED. It is the committed illustrative demo artefact,
# it carries a marker in its name saying it is not a client, and serving it is the point of
# this container. Compose mounts it READ-ONLY so a running container cannot dirty the copy
# that is committed.

# Local scratch and logs. `.scratch/` is gitignored working space; logs are noise.
.scratch
*.log
logs/

# --- Things the image does not need ---
#
# `node_modules` is rebuilt inside the image by `npm ci`, and copying the host's would ship
# whatever platform and whatever dev dependencies this machine happens to have.
node_modules

# The tests, and the harness they use. NOT EXCLUDED BECAUSE TESTS ARE SECRET: because they
# are not part of the running application, they pull in `puppeteer` in some paths, and an
# image that can run its own test suite is an image that ships an attack surface nobody
# asked it to serve. `npm test` runs on the host.
test

# The repository's own history and tooling. `.git` is large, and nothing in the image reads
# it. The compose file and the Dockerfile itself are not needed inside the image: compose
# reads them on the host.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Documentation and specs. Present in the repo for people, not for the running app.
*.md
SPEC-three-workflows.md
NOTES-client-coverage.md
NOTES-deepseek-json-mode.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp
